We can ship a patch to the compatibility layer: on parse, if arguments is an array:
1) if array[0] is string -> try JSON.parse
2) if array[0] is object -> use it
3) else -> fallback error. I'll open a PR and roll to staging.

Example code snippet we can add in node runtime:

```js
function normalizeArgs(args) {
  if (Array.isArray(args) && args.length === 1) {
    const a0 = args[0];
    if (typeof a0 === 'string') {
      try { return JSON.parse(a0); } catch(e) { throw new Error('arg parse failed'); }
    }
    if (typeof a0 === 'object') return a0;
  }
  return args;
}
```
